  body: "# Payment to another person to protect a beneficiary\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe DMG describes
    directing all or part of benefit to another individual when necessary to protect the interests of a beneficiary
    or dependant.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThis payment direction is distinct from the appointment procedure.
    The captured paragraph requires an individual payee and excludes corporate bodies in this route; do not transfer
    that condition to all appointees.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 08300, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=37)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n- [DMG 08302, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66fd5bbbe84ae1fd8592ecf1/dmg-chapter-8-payment-of-benefit-and-deductions-from-benefit.pdf#page=37)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 8: Payment of benefit and deductions from benefit .\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch8` PDF SHA-256: `8bf08435715020c8cc57be24e06e6fd8c90d99232254004ba67d1c5dfc3dd864`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `e6c5a71afbf2536bc63a91a4389284b2b6b8aaaa8bff015d4f34b478f77b28cc`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-benefit-payment-arrangements
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source describes a direction changing who receives payment on behalf of the beneficiary.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch8/0037
      quote: "08300 The Secretary of State may direct that all or part of a claimant’s benefit entitlement be paid
        to\nanother person on behalf of the beneficiary where it is necessary to protect the interests of the\n\n\
        beneficiary or the dependant for whom the benefit is paid 1.\n\n\n                                     \
        \                                               1 SS (C&P) Regs, reg 34(1)"
      locator: DMG 08300
  - target: term/dmg-appointee
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: 'The two procedures are related by their role in acting or receiving payment for a claimant, but
      the cited provisions differ: an appointment application can come from a body, whereas this payee must be an
      individual.'
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch8/0034
      quote: "08251 The application must be in writing1 and can be from a\n\n\n1. person who is at least 18 years
        old2 or\n\n\n2. body of people, for example a firm of solicitors, a Housing Authority or a LA but not an
        officer of such a\n\ngroup named by their title only (for example, Finance Director) 3.\n\n\n          \
        \                                              1 SS (C&P) Regs, reg 33(1); 2 reg 33(1); 3 R(SB) 2/87"
      locator: DMG 08251
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch8/0037
      quote: "08302 The person who the Secretary of State directs that payment should be made to must be an\n\n\
        individual, benefit can not be paid to corporate bodies, for example a firm of solicitors 1.\n\n\n     \
        \                                                                                 1 SS (C&P) Regs, reg 34"
      locator: DMG 08302
